---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const LINKEDIN = "https://www.linkedin.com/in/saitgumus";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Sait Gumus — capital markets & securities infrastructure, cloud-native engineering, MKK and Trendyol experience."
>
  <article class="space-y-8">
    <header class="space-y-3">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-sky-400/90">
        Capital markets &amp; securities infrastructure
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">About</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-zinc-400">
        How I work in regulated financial systems, large-scale product orgs, and the day-to-day craft of shipping
        dependable software.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div
      class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-zinc-100"
    >
      <p>
        I’m <strong>Sait Gumus</strong>, a software engineer focused on <strong>capital markets and securities
        infrastructure</strong>. I currently work as a Software Engineer at <strong>MKK</strong> (Merkezi Kayıt
        Kuruluşu — Turkey’s central securities depository), building and evolving systems where correctness, auditability,
        and operational resilience matter as much as feature delivery.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that, I was a Software Developer at <strong>Trendyol Group</strong>, where I learned how high-traffic
        product engineering, platform boundaries, and delivery discipline come together in practice. That background
        shapes how I approach <strong>scalable backends</strong>, <strong>cloud-native</strong> services, and{" "}
        <strong>end-to-end ownership</strong> from design through deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technically, I’m comfortable across <strong>Golang</strong>, <strong>Spring Boot</strong>, <strong>Node.js</strong>,{" "}
        <strong>Kotlin</strong>, <strong>React</strong>, <strong>Kubernetes</strong>, <strong>Docker</strong>,{" "}
        <strong>PostgreSQL</strong>, <strong>Elasticsearch</strong>, and patterns such as{" "}
        <strong>microservices</strong>, <strong>event-driven</strong> design, and <strong>CI/CD</strong>—always with an
        emphasis on <strong>clean, maintainable</strong> code that teams can extend without surprises.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of work, I’m a <strong>father of two</strong>, a lifelong learner, and someone who cares about clear
        thinking and systems that stay useful after the first release. I write longer notes on the{" "}
        <a href="/blog/">blog</a> and keep selected work on the <a href="/projects/">projects</a> page.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Connect:</strong>{" "}
        <a href={LINKEDIN} rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
